tg wrote:
> What do you generally do - make a wish right away or use it as a
> permanent light source?
>
I very much prefer to have a permanent light source.  I find it
annoying to not have a light source and remembering to turn off my oil
lamps to save power annoys me.  Also, it means that I need to collect
regular lamps and deal with weight issues.  I guess it depends on how
long a game you expect to have, too.  At XL 10, your character is
sufficiently mature that you don't need the wish for survival as much
as finding a wish as a XL1.  With the exception of cross-class
artifacts, anything you wish for might just as easily turn up in the
dungeon and with reflection you're safe from lucky monsters weilding
wands of death.   For a low-level character (XL 1 -5) I'd go for the
wish - there's nothing quite like having +3 SDSM, +3 speed boots, and a
+3 cloak of MR at XL 3!

But if you'd really like to run with a wished-for-artifact with this
character then you won't be nearly as nervous of being gifted with an
artifact following sacrifices.  Personal experience: with my current
caveman I had hoped to wish for the Eye but I guess I forgot and
received Mojo from a sacrifice.  "oops, now I gotta just avoid being
crowned prior to the castle wand" ... logged on the next day and with
maxed out luck got crowned, received Vorpy and now I figure I won't
bother with wishing for an artifact.  Oh well.

It's a good problem too have though!  Lucky you!
